<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  A sidecar: JSBSim never reads this file. Which ArduCopter quad X output drives what (channel = SERVOn - 1). AP_MotorsMatrix assigns
  Motor1..4 to SERVO1..4 by itself; firmwares/ardupilot_stork.param adds SERVO5:

    SERVO1 Motor1 (33)  front right CCW  -> channel 0 -> propulsion/engine[0]/collective-ctrl-rad
    SERVO2 Motor2 (34)  rear left CCW    -> channel 1 -> propulsion/engine[3]/collective-ctrl-rad
    SERVO3 Motor3 (35)  front left CW    -> channel 2 -> propulsion/engine[1]/collective-ctrl-rad
    SERVO4 Motor4 (36)  rear right CW    -> channel 3 -> propulsion/engine[2]/collective-ctrl-rad
    SERVO5 Max (136)    always PWM 1900  -> channel 4 -> Motor index 0, i.e. fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0]: both turbines' governor

  The turbines, why a held channel: a quad frame has no RSC, and the shaft needs 4.9 s from rest to 99 % rpm (measured). SERVOn_FUNCTION 136
  outputs SERVOn_MAX from boot, armed or not (SRV_Channel_aux.cpp), so the rotors reach speed at flat pitch before the EKF lets the machine arm
  (41 s in SITL) and stay governed after it disarms, and ArduCopter's thrust curve holds from its first command. A row tied to arming would run
  the collective to PWM 1940 at 340 rpm (it lifted off at 423 rpm and still made the height), and nothing here needs Lua. ArduCopter
  cannot shut the engines down. The engine binding, not property=: PteroSim writes each engine's FCS throttle from its engine command every
  step, over any property binding. Engines 1 and 2, the turbines, need no binding: Systems/stork_drive.xml writes their throttles, and
  PteroSim starts every engine.

  Signs, measured on the FDM alone (trimmed hover at 200 ft, controls frozen, +0.01 rad on one rotor against an unstepped twin, 1 kHz). Moment at 0.05 s, lb ft; ArduPilot's outputs are body FRD, + roll = right down, + pitch = nose UP, + yaw = nose right, and
  AP_MotorsMatrix's X factors want these signs for + output on the motor:
    Motor1 engine[0]  roll -822  pitch +859  yaw +56  (- + +): as wanted
    Motor2 engine[3]  roll +813  pitch -870  yaw +56  (+ - +): as wanted
    Motor3 engine[1]  roll +806  pitch +864  yaw -57  (+ + -): as wanted
    Motor4 engine[2]  roll -810  pitch -873  yaw -57  (- - -): as wanted
  So Propulsion.xml's sense +1 (CCW seen from above) is ArduPilot's CCW pair, and engine order is not ArduPilot's order.
  Range: PWM 1000..2000 reads 0..1 = 0.1175..0.5 rad, the FDM's own stops (stork.xml), all of it thrust a rotor can use on its own; held
  by the engine limit past about 0.42 rad with all four at it (droops to 489 rpm and 6929 lb in total at the stop, sea level). Zero thrust
  at 0.155 rad = PWM 1097; DGW hover at sea level 0.3173 rad = PWM 1522, at 6200 ft 0.3416 rad = PWM 1586.
-->
<control_bindings stack="ArduPilot">
  <binding stack="ArduPilot" channel="0" property="propulsion/engine[0]/collective-ctrl-rad" in="0 1" out="0.1175 0.5" label="front_right"/>
  <binding stack="ArduPilot" channel="1" property="propulsion/engine[3]/collective-ctrl-rad" in="0 1" out="0.1175 0.5" label="rear_left"/>
  <binding stack="ArduPilot" channel="2" property="propulsion/engine[1]/collective-ctrl-rad" in="0 1" out="0.1175 0.5" label="front_left"/>
  <binding stack="ArduPilot" channel="3" property="propulsion/engine[2]/collective-ctrl-rad" in="0 1" out="0.1175 0.5" label="rear_right"/>
  <binding stack="ArduPilot" channel="4" type="Motor" index="0" in="0 1" out="0 1" label="turbine"/>
</control_bindings>
